# The readers of topo's cover doors (scripts/gates/cover-kind-match.sh): one
# line per file, enclosing fn and door, tab-separated: FILE, FN (qualified
# `Type::name` or numbered `name#2` where a file declares it twice), DOOR,
# the COUNT of references, the DIRECTION it reads looseness in, and the
# argument for it. Directions: prunes (a looser cover costs work, never an
# answer); refuses (looser refuses more, never grants wrongly); examines
# (looser sends more to an exact reading); two-sided (the bound must be the
# entity's own: either way is a different answer; every lever whose
# consumer reads both signs is one, since Margin::levered is x times the
# arm); namesake (the token names another item). A new reader, or a swap
# of one door for another in a fn, lands by adding its line; a reader that
# goes drops its line.
crates/editor-core/src/eval/measure.rs	reach_of	face_cover	1	two-sided	a face's farthest distance from a part origin is the lever of a parallelism tilt: the measure grants parallel only on Zero and refuses on nonzero, but the mate solve, the at-rest check and the wire pose read it too and grant a non-parallel verdict on nonzero, so a bigger cover reads in-band tilts as decided there; a smaller one certifies a parallelism that does not hold.
crates/editor-core/src/eval/wire/trace.rs	drawn	face_cover	1	refuses	a traced face carries its cover for the plane-miss read: a bigger cover is shown to miss less often and hands off to the exact crossing, never a wrong miss
crates/editor-core/src/names/emit_union.rs	Flush::of	edge_cover	1	namesake	the token is Flush::edge_cover, the flush record's own method over its incidence table, which reads no cover of topo's: a namesake, so no direction applies
crates/sweep/src/blend/reach.rs	sheet_clip	face_cover	1	refuses	a revolve face's cover and nearest distance in the sheet frame bound where the blend band can reach: a bigger cover meters more cells and refuses as uncertified sooner, never prunes a reachable face
crates/sweep/src/blend/reach.rs	sheet_clip	face_nearest	1	refuses	a revolve face's cover and nearest distance in the sheet frame bound where the blend band can reach: a bigger cover meters more cells and refuses as uncertified sooner, never prunes a reachable face
crates/topo/src/boolean/arcs.rs	arcs_along	edge_cover_linked	1	two-sided	the arc's farthest reach from its vertex levers its tangent's tilt, and the arc is along a direction only on a Zero tilt: a longer arm rules out an arc the band holds along the tangent, a shorter one reads a departing arc as along it
crates/topo/src/boolean/carrier_pair.rs	face_ball	face_cover	1	two-sided	the face's cover ball is the consumed extent the carrier doors lever their tilts over, and they grant on either sign (one carrier on Zero, distinct on nonzero): Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner; no cover refuses the pair
crates/topo/src/boolean/carrier_touch.rs	edge_clear_of_ball	centred_box	1	prunes	an edge box clear of the touch ball's box is clear at once, any other is decided on its floor: a bigger box costs that floor, and refuses only where the edge has none
crates/topo/src/boolean/carrier_touch.rs	edge_clear_of_ball	edge_box	1	prunes	an edge box clear of the touch ball's box is clear at once, any other is decided on its floor: a bigger box costs that floor, and refuses only where the edge has none
crates/topo/src/boolean/fate.rs	leaving	edge_reach_bounds	1	refuses	the edge's reach from its base is read as bounds, and the departure decides only where both bounds agree (decide_levered); the margin is monotone in the arm, so a bigger cover can only turn agreement into a straddle, which refuses, never a different sign
crates/topo/src/boolean/glue.rs	overlapping_pairs	face_box	1	prunes	both operands' face boxes feed the glue sweep: a loose box only adds pairs the carrier ladder reads and leaves apart
crates/topo/src/boolean/glue.rs	section_door	cover_box	1	two-sided	every face's cover is boxed and the operands' hulls meet within the band as the operation's region, which bounds the section's trace and levers its pose decisions (parallel or coaxial on Zero, transverse on nonzero, both read): Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner; a narrower region misses section points
crates/topo/src/boolean/glue.rs	section_door	face_cover	1	two-sided	every face's cover is boxed and the operands' hulls meet within the band as the operation's region, which bounds the section's trace and levers its pose decisions (parallel or coaxial on Zero, transverse on nonzero, both read): Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner; a narrower region misses section points
crates/topo/src/boolean/glue.rs	section_door	hull_of_covers	1	two-sided	every face's cover is boxed and the operands' hulls meet within the band as the operation's region, which bounds the section's trace and levers its pose decisions (parallel or coaxial on Zero, transverse on nonzero, both read): Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner; a narrower region misses section points
crates/topo/src/boolean/glue.rs	section_door	meet_within	1	two-sided	every face's cover is boxed and the operands' hulls meet within the band as the operation's region, which bounds the section's trace and levers its pose decisions (parallel or coaxial on Zero, transverse on nonzero, both read): Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner; a narrower region misses section points
crates/topo/src/boolean/join.rs	cone_reach	cone_face_reach	1	two-sided	a cone face's reach from the germ levers the plane-cone section's pose, read on Zero and nonzero alike: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/boolean/join.rs	cone_window	face_cover	1	two-sided	a cone face's cover narrows the cone reach's window, and that reach levers the plane-cone pose read on either sign: a wider window lengthens the arm and decides nonzero sooner, a narrower one than the section's reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/boolean/join.rs	face_reach	face_reach_from	1	two-sided	a torus face's reach from the germ levers the plane-torus frame's pose, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/boolean/join.rs	frame_extent	face_axial_range	1	two-sided	a wall's axial range and reach from the germ lever its frame's pose decisions, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/boolean/join.rs	frame_extent	face_reach_from	1	two-sided	a wall's axial range and reach from the germ lever its frame's pose decisions, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/boolean/mod.rs	boolean_reduce_declared_strategy	face_box	1	prunes	the held-pierce read's curved face boxes: a face whose box clears the pierce point is not asked, any other is decided on its residual and trim
crates/topo/src/boolean/mod.rs	witness_span	face_cover	1	examines	each face's cover's range along the tangent line bounds the witness span: a bigger range admits a pair to the exact line reading and lengthens the metered span, which only refuses more
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	ball_may_reach	face_box	2	refuses	the approximated-face fallback refuses unless the ball's extent clears the face box: a bigger box refuses a separated pair as CurvedBooleanUnsupported
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	face_boundary_meets	edge_box	1	refuses	a plane face's boundary edge boxes against the section circle's box: a bigger box sends the pair to FallbackExtentUnsupported unless the narrow phase parts it
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	face_rows	cover_box	1	examines	one box per face for the section certificate's pair scan: a loose box sends a separated pair through the classification and lengthens its reach lever
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	face_rows	face_cover	1	examines	one box per face for the section certificate's pair scan: a loose box sends a separated pair through the classification and lengthens its reach lever
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	gate	face_box	3	refuses	the cylinder-face arm clears a face box against the ball's extent before refusing by kind: a bigger box refuses an operation whose faces never meet
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	overlap_reach	meet_within	1	two-sided	two faces' covers met within the band are the section certificate's reach, which pivots and levers the angular margins the classification reads on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner; a narrower one misses the section
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	sphere_extent_scan	centred_box	1	refuses	the sphere ball's box and each section circle's box decide the extent fallback: a bigger box turns a separated pair into a typed refusal
crates/topo/src/boolean/ops.rs	sphere_extent_scan	circle_box	1	refuses	the sphere ball's box and each section circle's box decide the extent fallback: a bigger box turns a separated pair into a typed refusal
crates/topo/src/boolean/overlap.rs	half_plane	piece_reach_bounds	1	refuses	a piece's reach from the overlap point is read as bounds, and the half-plane side decides only where both bounds agree; the margin is monotone in the arm, so a bigger cover only turns agreement into a straddle, which refuses
crates/topo/src/boolean/reduce.rs	face_tree	face_box	1	prunes	the C10 candidate tree over face boxes: loose is slower work, never a different answer
crates/topo/src/boolean/reduce.rs	first_unsupported_pair	face_box	2	refuses	the operand gate grants on non-overlap of an unsupported face's box: a bigger box refuses an operation unless the narrow phase parts the pair
crates/topo/src/boolean/reduce.rs	gate_maximal_faces	edge_cover_linked	1	two-sided	an edge cover's farthest distance from its start levers the maximal-faces plane test, which passes on Distinct (nonzero) and refuses on one plane or undecided: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, so a bigger cover passes a near-coplanar pair the true edge reads in band
crates/topo/src/boolean/reduce.rs	sweep_direction	edge_box	2	prunes	edge boxes in the C10 tree's edge pass: loose is slower work, never a different answer
crates/topo/src/boolean/ruled_region.rs	ruled_face_region	edge_cover	1	two-sided	each boundary edge's cover bounds a ruled face's scale, the lever of its crossing sines: every Zero abandons the path, and a decided sine places a crossing, so a bigger cover places crossings the true scale reads in band, a smaller one abandons paths it decides
crates/topo/src/boolean/solid_contain.rs	partial_reach	face_reach_from	1	refuses	a face's reach from the ray anchor sizes the skip question's lever: a bigger cover lengthens it and refuses more
crates/topo/src/boolean/solid_contain.rs	selection_reach	face_reach_from	1	two-sided	each face's reach from the query point levers the parallel-ray gate: Zero runs the ray along the carrier (skip or abandon), nonzero reads a crossing, so a bigger cover reads a crossing for a ray the true reach holds along the carrier, a smaller one skips a ray that crosses
crates/topo/src/census.rs	Candidates::build	edge_box	2	prunes	the pre-filter's face and edge boxes and pass two's curved-edge boxes feed the census trees: a loose box only admits more pairs to the exact sweeps
crates/topo/src/census.rs	Candidates::build	face_box	1	prunes	the pre-filter's face and edge boxes and pass two's curved-edge boxes feed the census trees: a loose box only admits more pairs to the exact sweeps
crates/topo/src/census.rs	backstop_apart	face_cover_toward	1	refuses	the backstop's aimed covers clear a pair on a definitely negative margin against a containing box: over-width costs probes, never a wrong clear
crates/topo/src/census.rs	collinear_overlaps	edge_box	1	prunes	line edges' boxes give the coincident-edge pass its candidates: a loose box hands the parallel screen more pairs, which it parts
crates/topo/src/census.rs	curved_same_side_pairs	face_cover	1	refuses	each cylinder face's cover's range along the first's axis is its axial span: a looser span overlaps where the faces are apart and sends the pair to Door 1
crates/topo/src/census.rs	face_reach_in	face_cover	1	refuses	the face's cover's box at the census scalar clears instance pairs only on a definitely negative margin: over-width costs probes, never a wrong clear
crates/topo/src/census.rs	flush_at_rest	face_box	1	prunes	a tree over planar, cylinder and sphere face boxes whose overlaps are flush candidates: a loose box only adds candidates, each read exactly
crates/topo/src/census.rs	tangent_sectors	face_reach_from	1	two-sided	a face's reach from the touch point levers the tangent fan's sector comparisons, which decide touch or overlap on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner
crates/topo/src/census/curved.rs	tangent_on_interior	edge_reach_bounds	1	refuses	the edge's reach from the point is read as bounds, and the departure decides only where both bounds agree; the margin is monotone in the arm, so a bigger cover only turns agreement into a straddle, which leaves the pair unread
crates/topo/src/census/depth_gap.rs	face_read	face_cover	1	refuses	each face's cover's distance range from an axis or a centre clears on a depth gap: a looser cover raises the greatest depth and lowers the least, refusing a pair that is apart
crates/topo/src/census/depth_gap.rs	least_on	face_nearest	2	refuses	a face's nearest distance where its least lies on the boundary: a looser reading lowers the least depth, refusing a pair that is apart
crates/topo/src/census/in_plane.rs	standing	edge_cover	1	refuses	a curved edge's cover's support must lie definitely off the plane: a looser cover asks more of the edge and refuses a pair that is apart
crates/topo/src/chart_region.rs	pair_cover	face_cover	1	refuses	each face's cover read along the planes' normals and the cylinders' axes lengthens the margin and transfer lever: the pair declines or escalates more, never accepts
crates/topo/src/chord_join.rs	section_reach	cone_face_reach	1	two-sided	the section table's plane-cylinder, plane-cone and plane-torus arms read the face's axial range and reach as the pose's lever, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/chord_join.rs	section_reach	face_axial_range	1	two-sided	the section table's plane-cylinder, plane-cone and plane-torus arms read the face's axial range and reach as the pose's lever, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/chord_join.rs	section_reach	face_reach_from	2	two-sided	the section table's plane-cylinder, plane-cone and plane-torus arms read the face's axial range and reach as the pose's lever, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner, a shorter one reads a decided tilt in band
crates/topo/src/face_boxes.rs	of	face_box	1	prunes	every face's box in one tree for the blend's reach meter: loose only adds candidates and cells until the per-face cell budget refuses as uncertified
crates/topo/src/face_reach.rs	face_extent	face_reach_from	1	two-sided	a face's reach from a vertex levers the split's coplanarity and sense residuals: Zero grants parallel to the split plane and nonzero a side, so an under-claim decides Zero wrongly (the docs' named risk) and an over-claim decides a side for a face the true extent holds in band
crates/topo/src/link.rs	cleared	face_reach_from	1	two-sided	a face's far reach from the link point levers the link fan's wedges beside the radius, compared on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner
crates/topo/src/pieces.rs	of	face_box	4	prunes	the piece sort's screen over the result's face boxes: two shells whose boxes clear are never probed against each other; a bigger box costs a probe
crates/topo/src/pieces.rs	pieces_of	face_box	2	prunes	the boolean's exit builds the face-box closure the screen reads: a bigger box costs a probe, never an answer
crates/topo/src/pieces.rs	sort_into_pieces	face_box	2	prunes	the screen's face boxes for each shell: a bigger box costs a point-in-solid probe, never an answer
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	apart	face_cover	1	refuses	the narrow phase reads each face's cover's support along a direction that turns with the pair: where it grants, a looser cover closes a gap that parts the pair
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	apart_along	face_cover	3	refuses	each face's cover's support along a candidate axis: a looser cover closes a gap that parts the pair, so it refuses a grant
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	apart_by	face_cover	2	refuses	the narrow phase's axes between two anchors, read on each face's cover: a looser cover closes a gap that parts the pair
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	cover	edge_cover	1	refuses	an item's cover, face or edge, that the narrow phase reads its supports off: looser closes a gap that parts the pair
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	cover	face_cover	2	refuses	an item's cover, face or edge, that the narrow phase reads its supports off: looser closes a gap that parts the pair
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	span_by	face_cover	2	refuses	a face's cover's span along an axis: looser overlaps where the items are apart, refusing the grant
crates/topo/src/separating.rs	support_along	face_cover	1	refuses	a face's cover's support along a direction: looser reaches further and closes a separating gap, refusing the grant
crates/topo/src/separation.rs	Separation::of	face_box	1	refuses	both separation certificates grant on box non-overlap: a loose box withholds a certificate it should have given, never manufactures one
crates/topo/src/separation.rs	SolidSeparation::of	face_box	1	refuses	both separation certificates grant on box non-overlap: a loose box withholds a certificate it should have given, never manufactures one
crates/topo/src/session_box.rs	body_reach	edge_cover	1	refuses	each edge's cover along the world axes bounds the body's largest coordinate from below: exact on lines and circle arcs, so the box refuses only on a true lower bound
crates/topo/src/shell.rs	edge_box_in	edge_cover_linked	1	refuses	each edge's cover box in the face's plane builds the wall-clearance footprint: a bigger footprint sends a clearing pair to the wall reading, which refuses
crates/topo/src/shell.rs	moved_walls	edge_cover_linked	1	prunes	each wall's box from its edges' covers: walls whose boxes are apart are never read for a crossing; a bigger box costs that reading and lengthens its lever
crates/topo/src/shell/tests/footprint_fuzz.rs	every_arc_lies_in_its_footprint_box	edge_cover_over	1	examines	a fuzz row's oracle reads the edge's cover over a span to check the footprint box holds the arc: it decides nothing
crates/topo/src/splitting/classify.rs	edge_clears	edge_cover	1	refuses	an unarmed edge's cover in the plane's frame: a looser box reaches the plane and refuses the cut by kind
crates/topo/src/splitting/containment.rs	arc_distance_floor	arc_cover	1	refuses	the arc's cover's nearest distance is the floor the cell door and touch gate clear on: a looser cover lowers the floor and clears less, never a wrong clear
crates/topo/src/splitting/containment.rs	step_cover	edge_cover	1	two-sided	each edge's cover folded into a ball about the point levers the point-in-loop crossing decisions, read on either sign: Margin::levered is x times the arm, so a longer arm leaves Zero sooner and decides nonzero sooner
crates/topo/src/validate.rs	ring_pairs	edge_box	1	prunes	two rings of one face whose hulled edge boxes clear are never handed to the contact arms: a bigger box costs a pair the exact arms
crates/topo/src/validate.rs	side	edge_reach_bounds	1	refuses	a conic or spiric edge's reach from its start is read as bounds, and the departure decides only where both bounds agree; the margin is monotone in the arm, so a bigger cover only turns agreement into a straddle, which refuses
